g++ --std=c++11 -c VerletGravitySimEfficient.cpp -I/usr/include/SFML-2.6.1/include && g++ VerletGravitySimEfficient.o -o App -L/usr/include/SFML-2.6.1/lib -lsfml-graphics -lsfml-window -lsfml-system -lsfml-audio && export LD_LIBRARY_PATH=/usr/include/SFML-2.6.1/lib && ./App



just compile and run this and watch as the Verlet simulation takes some "orbees" and makes them collide. 

If you'd like to make the balls more squishy, change the "squishval" to anything less than 1.f for a more forgiving collision resolution

To be clear, this is an N body simulation with collisions, so it is a bit slow
